WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:00.567
Tonight, the

00:00:00.567 --> 00:00:01.167
man who spent

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.936
decades helping run Donald

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:03.703
Trump's family

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:05.772
business, Allen Weisselberg,

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:06.639
could be on the verge

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:09.242
of pleading guilty for the second time,

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:11.244
this time to a perjury charge,

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:12.312
we are told.

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:13.279
The 76 year old

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:14.314
was the chief financial

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:15.515
officer of the Trump

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:17.417
Organization for decades.

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:18.685
He went to jail at Rikers

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:20.787
for about 100 days last year.

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:21.955
That was for his role

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:22.455
in running

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:24.924
a 15 year tax fraud scheme

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:26.726
at the Trump Organization.

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:27.694
Now, tonight,

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:28.762
there is new reporting

00:00:28.762 --> 00:00:29.863
from The New York Times

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:31.364
and confirmed by CNN

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:32.699
that Weisselberg is in talks

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:34.534
to potentially plead guilty

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:36.169
to a perjury charge,

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:37.637
this time related to Trump's

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:39.139
civil fraud trial,

00:00:39.139 --> 00:00:41.041
where he, Allen Weisselberg,

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:41.975
would have to admit

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:43.743
that he lied on the stand

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:45.311
during his own testimony.

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:46.813
The timing here is also key

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:48.048
as we are learning more

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:49.482
about this new reporting,

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:50.150
because right now

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:52.118
we're waiting on the judge in this case

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:52.619
to decide

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:53.920
what the penalty is,

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.656
essentially how much Donald Trump owes

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:57.357
or reminder,

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:58.191
the attorney general

00:00:58.191 --> 00:00:59.392
in the closing arguments

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:02.729
after north of $370 million

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:03.630
and is a ruling

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:04.697
that could threaten Trump's

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:07.300
entire real estate empire.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.735
I'm joined tonight by the senior

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:10.937
editor at Forbes, Dan Alexander,

00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:12.639
who is the guest on this story,

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:13.773
because it was his reporting

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:14.941
that exposed

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:16.676
Weisselberg's alleged lies

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:17.977
under oath on the stand.

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:19.913
And then when you look at this

00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:21.614
and we don't know, I should note

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:23.049
which statement exactly

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:23.450
it is

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:24.517
that that could potentially

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:26.219
go towards this perjury charge

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:28.121
if he does plead guilty here.

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:29.522
But you noted in your reporting

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.825
that there were emails and notes from him

00:01:31.825 --> 00:01:32.559
that are believed to be

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:34.160
at the center of this.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.562
What did you pick up on

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:38.164
and what you believe that he lied about

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:38.765
as he was kind of

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:39.999
trying to distance himself from

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:43.503
Trump's financial statements?

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:44.971
Yes, I remember the trial.

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:45.772
It was about Trump

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:47.207
lying about his net worth.

00:01:47.207 --> 00:01:48.508
And one of the key

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:50.410
examples of that is that

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:51.277
Trump was claiming

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:54.147
that his penthouse was 30,000 square feet

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:58.418
when in fact it was 10,996 square feet.

00:01:58.518 --> 00:02:00.386
And Allen Weisselberg was on the stand

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:01.921
and was trying to explain

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:02.922
that he really had

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:04.424
nothing to do with this.

00:02:04.424 --> 00:02:07.160
And as he was making that claim,

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.762
it was obvious to me that he was lying.

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:11.264
I went back through our notes

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:14.267
and could track years of conversations

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:14.901
that he had had

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:15.768
with our reporters

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:17.604
where he was really focused

00:02:17.604 --> 00:02:19.038
on the penthouse,

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:20.273
where he was trying to claim

00:02:20.273 --> 00:02:21.274
that it was 30,000

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:23.910
square feet or even 33,000 square feet.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:26.212
I think at one point Donald Trump had it

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:27.347
and that he was trying to claim

00:02:27.347 --> 00:02:29.516
that it was wildly overvalued.

00:02:29.516 --> 00:02:32.318
So this is clear documented stuff

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:33.786
that you can say,

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:35.421
you know, he's claiming one number.

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:37.423
The documents show another number

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:38.725
and he's lying.

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:38.992
You know,

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:40.426
you noted in that story

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:41.861
that you had documents

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:44.130
that prosecutors didn't have.

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:45.031
Did you hear from their

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:48.501
office after that?

00:02:48.568 --> 00:02:50.603
So their office did

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:54.007
go back and look through documents

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:55.141
with the Trump Organization

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:56.109
and try to do an additional

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:57.744
sort of forensic look.

00:02:57.744 --> 00:02:58.344
And they

00:02:58.344 --> 00:03:00.647
put some paperwork in the docket

00:03:00.647 --> 00:03:01.915
about that.

00:03:01.915 --> 00:03:05.818
They did not come after us for anything

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:09.022
but everything that we have is out there.

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:11.157
You know, we've released tapes of Trump

00:03:11.157 --> 00:03:12.892
lying about the size of his penthouse.

00:03:12.892 --> 00:03:14.727
We've put out the notes

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:15.662
of Weisselberg's

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:17.797
conversations over the years.

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:20.166
All of this stuff has all been laid out

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:21.534
very clear.

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:23.670
It's a remarkable piece of journalism.

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:25.738
Dan Alexander, thank you for that.

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:27.407
And for more on this breaking story,

00:03:27.407 --> 00:03:29.075
we have former federal prosecutor

00:03:29.075 --> 00:03:30.677
Elie Honig here as well.

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:32.278
And you heard what Dan said there.

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:34.414
I mean, this is a groundbreaking article

00:03:34.414 --> 00:03:35.682
that pretty flatly stated

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:36.683
that they believed Allen

00:03:36.683 --> 00:03:38.818
Weisselberg had lied.

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:40.253
All of this is coming as Judge

00:03:40.253 --> 00:03:42.388
Negron has not decided yet.

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:43.790
He said by the jury,

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:44.991
obviously that was yesterday,

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:45.959
wasn't definitive.

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:47.293
But but could that play a role

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:48.595
in why we haven't heard from him yet?

00:03:48.595 --> 00:03:49.295
Absolutely.

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:50.863
If I'm in Judge and Gordon's

00:03:50.863 --> 00:03:51.464
position here

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:52.565
and getting ready to issue

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:53.933
a big verdict and ruling

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:54.867
and now I hear this

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:55.735
and now we've all heard it,

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:57.637
that one of the key witnesses

00:03:57.637 --> 00:03:59.272
committed perjury in front of me.

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:00.640
I slam on the brakes

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:01.908
and I say I'm not going to rule

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:03.910
until I know the specifics of this now.

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:05.111
I think it's likely the judge

00:04:05.111 --> 00:04:06.312
probably discredited

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:07.814
Allen Weisselberg's testimony

00:04:07.814 --> 00:04:09.382
anyway because it was contradicted

00:04:09.382 --> 00:04:10.416
by so many of the facts

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:11.751
as Dan just laid out.

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:13.086
But you have to know this as a judge,

00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:14.354
if you're going to issue a ruling

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:16.322
and if it turns out Weisselberg lied,

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:17.523
that's going to harm

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:18.458
the Trump Organization.

00:04:18.458 --> 00:04:19.792
When it comes time for the verdict,

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:20.593
how could it bode

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:22.562
for Donald Trump himself?

00:04:22.562 --> 00:04:23.997
It's a problem for Donald Trump

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:25.098
because he's going to be

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:26.766
on the receiving end of this verdict.

00:04:26.766 --> 00:04:27.400
It is important, though,

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:28.434
there's an important detail

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:29.469
in the reporting

00:04:29.469 --> 00:04:30.637
that Weisselberg's deal

00:04:30.637 --> 00:04:32.272
that he's working on or towards

00:04:32.272 --> 00:04:33.439
with prosecutors

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:33.973
does not

00:04:33.973 --> 00:04:35.642
necessarily involve

00:04:35.642 --> 00:04:36.476
Allen Weisselberg

00:04:36.476 --> 00:04:38.244
cooperating against Donald Trump.

00:04:38.244 --> 00:04:39.545
And that doesn't surprise me.

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:41.748
This guy is not in position to cooperate.

00:04:41.748 --> 00:04:42.682
I've I've cooperated

00:04:42.682 --> 00:04:44.183
some really bad guys.

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:45.084
But the problem is

00:04:45.084 --> 00:04:46.586
when you have an inveterate liar

00:04:46.586 --> 00:04:47.954
multiple times convicted,

00:04:47.954 --> 00:04:49.122
if he takes this plea,

00:04:49.122 --> 00:04:50.556
you can't put that person on the stand

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:51.958
and ask a jury to believe him.

00:04:51.958 --> 00:04:52.959
And also when we talk

00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:54.193
I mean, Allen Weisselberg

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:55.728
fiercely loyal to Donald Trump,

00:04:55.728 --> 00:04:56.262
I should note.

00:04:56.262 --> 00:04:57.597
But I think one thing we forget about,

00:04:57.597 --> 00:04:58.898
which The New York Times noted tonight,

00:04:58.898 --> 00:04:59.565
is that

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:01.467
he got a $2 million severance package

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:02.135
that required him

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:03.336
not to cooperate

00:05:03.336 --> 00:05:05.004
with any law enforcement investigation

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:06.372
unless he was legally required.

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:07.540
That was stunning to me.

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:09.142
I've never heard of such a thing.

00:05:09.142 --> 00:05:11.311
I don't think that's enforceable to say

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:13.446
you won't cooperate with law enforcement.

00:05:13.446 --> 00:05:14.747
I mean, it certainly undermines

00:05:14.747 --> 00:05:16.582
what prosecutors are trying to do.

00:05:16.582 --> 00:05:18.284
I mean, unless legally required that,

00:05:18.284 --> 00:05:19.452
I guess that could mean a subpoena

00:05:19.452 --> 00:05:20.320
for trial or anything.

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:22.655
But that's a shocking detail

00:05:22.655 --> 00:05:24.223
to put into a severance agreement

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:25.325
in addition to the amount.

00:05:25.325 --> 00:05:26.726
So they're clearly Trump

00:05:26.726 --> 00:05:27.126
and his people

00:05:27.126 --> 00:05:28.761
are trying to keep weisselberg

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:29.562
in the fold here,

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:29.762
I think,

00:05:29.762 --> 00:05:30.663
because they're worried about him

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:31.130
slipping.

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:32.131
Yeah, And I should note

00:05:32.131 --> 00:05:33.800
he has not actually agreed to this yet.

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:35.568
He's just in talks to potentially do so.

00:05:35.568 --> 00:05:36.469
It could fall apart.

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:37.036
We've seen it happen

00:05:37.036 --> 00:05:38.271
with other plea deals.

00:05:38.271 --> 00:05:38.538
L.A.

00:05:38.538 --> 00:05:40.273
Witness or Ali Hoenig,

00:05:40.273 --> 00:05:41.607
thank you, helped me with this.

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:43.009
So if I saw something,

00:05:43.009 --> 00:05:44.210
he would be a great witness.

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:44.844
Instead,

00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:45.945
I do want to turn now

00:05:45.945 --> 00:05:47.146
to conservative attorney

00:05:47.146 --> 00:05:48.348
and one of Donald Trump's

00:05:48.348 --> 00:05:49.082
fiercest critics

00:05:49.082 --> 00:05:50.016
who anyone who watches

00:05:50.016 --> 00:05:50.850
the source would know

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:52.151
George Conway is here.

00:05:52.151 --> 00:05:52.485
George,

00:05:52.485 --> 00:05:54.754
I mean, if this does come to fruition

00:05:54.754 --> 00:05:56.356
for Allen Weisselberg,

00:05:56.356 --> 00:05:58.157
the theme here would be in

00:05:58.157 --> 00:06:00.026
both guilty pleas that

00:06:00.026 --> 00:06:02.195
he was lying on Donald Trump's behalf,

00:06:02.195 --> 00:06:03.229
would it not?

00:06:03.229 --> 00:06:03.629
Yes.

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:05.832
And it's actually not surprising

00:06:05.832 --> 00:06:06.399
because that's

00:06:06.399 --> 00:06:08.334
what Donald Trump does to people.

00:06:08.334 --> 00:06:10.937
And we've seen numerous circumstances

00:06:10.937 --> 00:06:12.839
where Trump has gotten people to lie

00:06:12.839 --> 00:06:14.540
or obstruct justice

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:16.876
